course: dictionary
lesson: 5889
title: The mantis: a praying insect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mantis is a long green or brown insect. It is often called a praying mantis because it folds its spiky front legs together as if it is praying. Do not be fooled: it is waiting to catch its dinner.
explain: Mantises snatch other insects with those spiky front legs. They can also turn their heads right round to look behind them. «The orchid mantis looks like a flower, catches insects that come to it.»
explain: Animals that look like something else are using camouflage. Some look like leaves, sticks or flowers, so the creatures they hunt, and the animals that hunt them, may not spot them. Scientists study mantises to learn how camouflage and life cycles work.
fact: A mantis is a long green or brown insect with spiky front legs.
fact: A praying mantis gets its name from the way it folds its front legs together.
fact: Mantises can turn their heads right round to look behind them.
fact: «Ants, beetles, mantises and cockroaches have six legs and are insects.»
fact: Camouflage means looking like something else: «a stick insect looks like a twig».
exercise: What is a mantis? | *A long green or brown insect | A bird that looks like a broken stump | A type of tarantula | A fish that hides in seaweed
exercise: Why is it called a praying mantis? | It only moves on Sundays | It sings quietly before it eats | It has a face like a monk | *It folds its spiky front legs together as if praying
exercise: How many legs do mantises have? | Twelve | *Six | Eight | Four
test: «The orchid mantis looks like a flower, catches insects that come to it.» Why does the orchid mantis look like a flower? | To fly across the sea | To hide from the rain | *To catch insects that come to it | To turn its head right round
test: Which of these animals has eight legs, not six? | Ant | Mantis | *Tarantula | Beetle
exam: Mantises can turn their heads right round, and they have six legs. Which statement is true? | Mantises cannot move their heads | Mantises are a kind of spider | *Mantises are insects with six legs | Mantises have eight legs like tarantulas
